a226d94fe8c6fbfecb81de415feb645302cdd166:Blockchain/Dev/DEVELOPMENT.md:110:| G6 | ~~Verifier role can't actually verify~~ — ✅ fixed 2026-04-27 (option b). Gateway verify handler now does a 3-tier lookup: originate (owners get full record incl. revocation), then anchoring's `/api/anchors/document/:id` (any authed user — works for verifiers), then mock store. Verified end-to-end: verifier@secuura.com gets `verified: true, blockchainAnchored: true, source: cardano-live` against issuer@secuura.com's doc. Follow-up: revocation status is unavailable to non-owners; need a public revocation-list endpoint or on-chain revocation events for verifiers to see "this doc was revoked" properly. | ✅ |
a226d94fe8c6fbfecb81de415feb645302cdd166:Blockchain/Dev/DEVELOPMENT.md:121:| ~~H2~~ (was F-API-01 part 2) | — | `/api/anchors/document/:id` | ✅ FIXED | Now returns 404 with no echoed id when no anchors match. Verified: nonexistent id → `404 {"error":"No anchors found"}`; real id → 200 with full anchors array. Gateway's `makeFetchDocFromAnchorStore` already handles non-200 by resolving null, so verifier-portal flow is unaffected. |
a226d94fe8c6fbfecb81de415feb645302cdd166:Blockchain/Dev/DEVELOPMENT.md:151:| ~~H24~~ | — | `GET /api/anchors/document/:id` (carried from F-API-01) | ⚠ NOT-A-BUG (baseline-confirmed) | Conflicts with `Blockchain/Testing/baselines/06-tenant-isolation.txt` which baselines this route as by-design. Anchor metadata (txHash, blockHeight, contentHash, network) is publicly observable on Cardanoscan — verifier role's verify-by-id flow EXPECTS to read it. Test agent flagged it again because they ran through a checklist; no actual security gap. |
a226d94fe8c6fbfecb81de415feb645302cdd166:Blockchain/Dev/docs/SCOPES.md:43:| `anchors:read` | `GET /api/anchors/document/{id}` — poll anchor status. |
a226d94fe8c6fbfecb81de415feb645302cdd166:Blockchain/Dev/docs/diagrams/api-sequence-document-lifecycle.mmd:59:        Client->>GW: GET /api/anchors/document/documentId
